course: dictionary
lesson: 3899
title: Fridge: a cold cupboard for food
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fridge is a cold cupboard in the kitchen. It keeps food and drinks cool and fresh, usually at about 3 to 5 degrees Celsius. Fridge is short for refrigerator, so it is a shortened word, like many everyday words.
explain: Context helps you work out what fridge means. «Warmth makes yeast work faster, so dough is left somewhere warm; in a cold fridge it rises very slowly.» The word cold tells you that the fridge is cold, because a cold place is the opposite of warm.
explain: Try the swap check. Put "cold cupboard in the kitchen" in place of fridge in «Yoghurt is kept in the fridge so it does not go off.» Does it still make sense? If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: A fridge is a noun. The plural is fridges.
fact: «Fridge» means a cold cupboard in the kitchen that keeps food and drinks cool and fresh.
fact: Inside a fridge it is usually about 3 to 5 degrees Celsius.
fact: A freezer is much colder than a fridge, at about minus 18 degrees Celsius.
fact: Phrases to know: in the fridge, fridge door, fridge magnet, out of the fridge.
exercise: What is a fridge? | A table where you eat your tea | *A cold cupboard in the kitchen that keeps food and drinks cool and fresh | A hot oven for baking bread
exercise: Find the word in «In a cold fridge it rises very slowly» that tells you the fridge is cold. | slowly | dough | *cold | rises
exercise: Fridge is short for which longer word? | cupboard | *refrigerator | freezer | kitchen
test: The lesson says where raw meat should go in the fridge. Where is that? | On the kitchen table | *On the bottom shelf | On the top shelf, near the milk | In the fridge door, with the eggs
test: In a power cut, what should you do with the fridge? | Fill it with hot food | Turn it upside down | Open it wide to check the food | *Keep it closed
exam: Why does a fridge keep yoghurt from going off? | It makes the yoghurt hot | It turns yoghurt into cheese | It stops anyone from eating the yoghurt | *Cold slows down how fast food goes off
